# Design tokens for color

Single source of **CSS hex**: [`src/styles/mit-theme.css`](src/styles/mit-theme.css). Single source for **TS inline hex** (SVG, charts, rare `style=`): **`tokens.colors`** in [`src/lib/mit-sailing/tokens.ts`](src/lib/mit-sailing/tokens.ts). Institute palette reference: **[MIT Brand Guide — Color](https://brand.mit.edu/color)** — see [mit-brand-colors.mdc](mit-brand-colors.mdc).

- **Foreground text:** use **`text-foreground`** / **`text-mit-text`** or **`tokens.colors.text`** (`#09090b` in light mode, aligned with `:root --foreground`) for readable copy. For hierarchy, use **font size, weight, or spacing**, not unverified low-contrast gray.
- **Brand reds:** **`text-mit-red`**, **`bg-primary`**, **`tokens.colors.mitRed`** — optional **`mitRedBright`** for expanded-palette emphasis only.
- **New color roles:** add a CSS variable in `mit-theme.css`, wire it in `@theme inline`, then expose a **`tokens.colors`** field if TS needs the same value.

**Focus rings / arbitrary colors:** Align with **`text-mit-text`** / `--ring` (see `textFocusRingClassName`) rather than duplicating hex in many places.

**Authentication UI:** Use MIT theme utilities — see [mit-auth-ui-colors.mdc](mit-auth-ui-colors.mdc); avoid **`blue-*`** for primary actions and avoid raw MIT hex literals.
